  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 126 AM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nBroad ridging over South Central Texas early next week becomes more \namplified heading into the late week period. This pattern brings a \nday by day warming trend to the area through mid-week with \ntemperatures at or above average by Wednesday. Lows from the 40s and \n50s Monday morning rise into the 60s across the area by Friday. For \nhighs, Monday remains mild in the 70s to around 80 degrees, then \nrises into the 80s across the entire area by Thursday. A trough \nmoves over the western US in the late week period but the elongated \nupper ridge may limit impacts for our area associated with this \nfeature. For now, the forecast remains dry.",
